# DTF tier manifest: admin-setup-gate  (artifact-keeper#4634, fixed by #4635; 1.11.2)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The oracle restarts the backend twice
# (force-recreate on the same volume + database, with fixtures/setup.logs.yml
# for json-file logs) and edits the users table directly only to stage state
# an operator reaches through restarts and time.
#
# THE BUG
# The first-run setup gate (every route except /api/v1/auth/*, the setup
# status and the password-change route answers 403 SETUP_REQUIRED) is meant to
# be about the built-in `admin`. Before #4635 three places looked at ANY local
# admin instead:
#   * boot: provision_admin_user read `SELECT must_change_password, is_active
#     FROM users WHERE is_admin AND external_id IS NULL LIMIT 1` (no username,
#     no ORDER BY). With other admins created with a temporary password, the
#     row returned could be one of them: the gate armed, and with
#     <STORAGE_PATH>/admin.password missing the boot generated a random
#     password and wrote it to `admin`, replacing the operator's ADMIN_PASSWORD.
#   * runtime: AppState::setup_still_required re-checked "any active admin
#     pending", and update_user re-armed the latch when ANY pending local admin
#     was reactivated.
#   * runtime: change_password_inner dropped the latch when ANY user with a
#     pending flag rotated, even while `admin` was still pending.
# #4635 pins all of them to username = 'admin'.
#
# THE PHASES
#   setup     the seeded instance (admin from ADMIN_PASSWORD, nothing pending);
#             two admins P1, P2 created via POST /api/v1/users with a
#             generated password (must_change_password = true).
#   runtime   PATCH P1 is_active false, then true.
#   boot      re-touch the `admin` row until the pre-fix unordered lookup
#             returns a pending admin (each UPDATE writes a new heap tuple:
#             the field condition, staged deterministically), confirm no
#             admin.password exists, restart.
#   pre-setup flag `admin` must_change_password = true and restart: the gate
#             is armed by the built-in admin on both images; P2 logs in and
#             rotates its own password; then admin completes setup with the
#             password from admin.password.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      runtime: admin's GET /api/v1/users stays 200, an anonymous
#              repository list stays 200, setup_required stays false.
#              RED on 1.11.1: 403 SETUP_REQUIRED (latch re-armed, DB re-check
#              finds P1).
#   (FIX)      boot: setup_required false, admin logs in with ADMIN_PASSWORD,
#              the anonymous list is 200, no admin.password written, no
#              "Regenerating password" / "API is locked" log line.
#              RED on 1.11.1: setup_required true, admin login 401 (password
#              regenerated), 403 SETUP_REQUIRED, admin.password written.
#   (FIX)      pre-setup: after P2's rotation setup_required is still true and
#              the anonymous list is still 403 SETUP_REQUIRED.
#              RED on 1.11.1: the gate drops (setup_required false, 200).
#   (CONTROL)  both images: the seeded instance is past setup and a pending
#              admin gets 428 on its own requests; with `admin` pending a
#              restart arms the gate (true, 403 SETUP_REQUIRED, password file
#              readable); admin's own rotation lifts it and P1 still gets 428.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: about a dozen logins.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
